the fbi warns that the critical daily  functions of hospitals are at an  increased risk of being hacked and in  tonight's cyber safe parent we look at  what needs to be done to keep patients  safe  hospitals and health care organizations  are a vulnerable target for a cyber  attack lagging behind other industries  in cyber readiness  the fbi has warned of an increased and  imminent cyber crime threat to u.s  hospitals metro lieutenant alan larson  with the health care sector we have seen  a huge increase in the amount of attacks  that are targeting our health care  partners we've even had some local  hospitals and clinics here in clark  county that have been you know victims  of cyber attacks a worrisome aspect is  that critical health care components  from ct scans to medical devices to the  refrigerators that store blood for  surgery could be compromised what would  be the very worst case scenario is if  they were able to compromise in such a  way that they're able to shut off power  or shut down their systems you know  they're providing this critical care to  these patients that would be the most  devastating thing electronic health care  record systems are now the norm for  private patient information if that gets  compromised now you can re-victimize  those patients lieutenant larson  encourages cloud-based servers to keep a  layer of separation from on-premise  servers endpoint protection for  computers attached to company networks  and firewalls requiring double  verification for patient portal records  we also have a healthcare working group  where we work with the information  security officers from these different  health cares  hospitals things like that to be able to  give them pointers and tips on how they  can help increase their infrastructure  so that they don't become victims of you  know a cyber attack experts warn the  time is now for a shift in the thinking  and planning of hospital cyber defense  with a far greater value being placed on  cyber security in the health care sector  it's of the utmost importance  now you can find all of our previous  segments many with helpful cyber hygiene  tips for businesses and individuals over  on our website eightnewsnow.com under  cyber safe parent
 

